NeuralGate — Tech Stack
Language & Runtime

Python 3.11 — primary language for all services
asyncio — native Python async runtime for non-blocking request handling

API & Web Framework

FastAPI — async API framework for the edge layer and request entry point
Uvicorn — ASGI server that runs FastAPI in production
Pydantic v2 — request/response schema validation and serialization

Message Queue & Task Processing

Redis — in-memory store for health scores, pool state, rate limit counters, and circuit breaker state
Celery — distributed task queue for managing batch pool workers
Redis Streams — lightweight queue for async batch job dispatch

Model Serving (inference backend)

vLLM — LLM inference engine with PagedAttention and continuous batching
Hugging Face Transformers — model loading, tokenization, and config management
Hugging Face Hub — model registry and versioned model pulls
Triton Inference Server (optional) — GPU-optimized serving for non-LLM model variants

Vector Database & Retrieval

FAISS — local approximate nearest neighbor search for vector similarity
pgvector — PostgreSQL extension for vector storage in production
PostgreSQL — primary relational store for retrieval metadata and request logs
sentence-transformers — embedding generation for RAG retrieval pipeline

Observability

Prometheus — metrics collection (p95, p99, queue depth, GPU utilization, token throughput, error rate)
Grafana — dashboards for latency, pool health, fallback events, and GPU saturation
OpenTelemetry — distributed tracing across edge → router → pool → retrieval
structlog — structured JSON logging with request-level context propagation
Alertmanager — alert routing for OOM events, fallback triggers, latency breaches

Infrastructure & Cloud (AWS)

EC2 (g4dn.xlarge or g5.xlarge) — GPU instances for online and large-context serving pools
EC2 (t3.medium) — CPU instances for router, edge layer, and batch coordination
ElastiCache (Redis) — managed Redis for health scores and circuit breaker state
RDS (PostgreSQL) — managed database for retrieval metadata and request audit logs
S3 — model artifact storage and request payload archiving for shadow testing
ECS / EKS — container orchestration for pool autoscaling and service deployment
ALB (Application Load Balancer) — entry point before the edge layer
CloudWatch — infrastructure-level metrics and log aggregation
IAM — service-to-service authentication and secrets access control

Containerization & Deployment

Docker — containerized packaging of every service component
Docker Compose — local development and integration testing environment
Kubernetes (EKS) — production orchestration with HPA for pool autoscaling
Helm — Kubernetes manifest templating for environment-specific configs

Load Testing & Chaos Engineering

Locust — load testing with realistic traffic profiles (online, burst, mixed)
pytest — unit, integration, and regression test runner
pytest-asyncio — async test support for FastAPI and asyncio components
httpx — async HTTP client for integration tests against live endpoints

Rollout & Experimentation

Custom shadow mode — built in rollout/shadow_mode.py, forks live traffic to new model versions without user impact
Custom canary engine — built in rollout/canary.py, shifts traffic percentage with auto-rollback on metric breach
Feature flags via Redis — runtime toggling of fallback tiers, hedged requests, and speculative decoding

Config & Secrets Management

YAML configs — pool config, fallback tiers, routing rules, alert thresholds (in configs/)
python-dotenv — local .env loading for secrets and environment variables
AWS Secrets Manager — production secrets for API keys, DB credentials, model tokens

